  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "About",
      "text": "Use the ratio helper to manage the aspect ratios of external content like\n`<iframe>`s, `<embed>`s, `<video>`s, and `<object>`s. These helpers also can be used on\nany standard HTML child element (e.g., a `<div>` or `<img>`). Styles are applied from\nthe parent .ratio class directly to the child.\n\nYou don't need to include `frameborder=\"0\"` in your `iframe`s.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Aspect ratios",
      "text": "Aspect ratios can be customized using `aspectRatio`. By default the following `aspectRatio`\nvalues are provided:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Custom",
      "text": "Create custom aspect ratios by passing a number to `aspectRatio` instead of using the above\npre-defined values. You can use either a fraction or percentage to define the custom ratio.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
